            "content": [
              {
                "annotations": [],
                "text": "An analysis of the training examples reveals the following rule:\n1. Find the non-zero color $C$ used in the 3x3 input grid.\n2. Invert the input grid by swapping 0 and $C$ (every 0 becomes $C$, and every $C$ becomes 0).\n3. Compute the Kronecker product (fractal expansion) of this inverted 3x3 grid with itself to produce the 9x9 output grid. That is, the 9x9 output is a 3x3 grid of 3x3 blocks; wherever the inverted grid has color $C$, place a copy of the inverted 3x3 grid, and wherever it has 0, place a 3x3 block of zeros.\n\nI am ready for the test input.",
